A||||6||86SE||How do you change the color of the dash lights?||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||04-25-2000||06:49 PM||||I gettin tired of the orange backlit dash panels and was wondering, is there was any way to change the color of the illumination?<P>I think green whould look cool......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||04-26-2000||01:39 AM||||I wish I knew...I would like to have the dash lights match my aftermarket sterio head unit.||||reg||9
Z||000002||CUTTER||04-26-2000||01:43 AM||||same here!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||04-26-2000||05:13 AM||||Like most dash lights im sure there is a orange cover over each light in the dash. Take off the cluster and pull off the covers. Then replace the bulbs with green ones (that you can get at most auto parts stores)..||||reg||14
Z||000004||Monkeyman||04-26-2000||09:27 AM||||If you get (or have) the backlit style of gauges, you can get SXMs gauge faces.  Seems like I remember they were less than $100 for the set.  Different colors for the faces and for the backlight.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||04-26-2000||11:24 AM||||Seeing as how I just tore my reflector gauges apart last weekend to install the white face decals, I can tell you that there are no orange-colored covers over each of the lamps.  To achieve the orange illumination, the backside of the black frame that covers the gauges is painted fluorescent orange, as is the back of the speedo face.<P>To change the color, I believe it'd be as simple as painting over the fluorescent orange paint with another fluorescent color.<P>Keep in mind, however, that most owners of the reflector style gauges complain about their lack of brightness.  Changing to a color other than say yellow or white will only make things worse.<P>Can't say for certain but I'd be willing to bet the backlit gauges are similar, only incorporating faces that are made from transparent orange plastic with a black coating.  As Monkeyman stated, purchasing a set of SXM's gauge faces with an alternate color is an option.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 04-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||superXmotorsports||04-26-2000||02:01 PM||||The SuperSport gauges that we sell look best with the red backlighting.  The red ones glow about as bright as stock.  The blue and green are a little dimmer.  We also sell red and orange faces with white or yellow lighting.  Thanks!  SXM.||||reg||1
